Diagnosis: the incumbent makes a single blind call — no execution feedback, no schema grounding, and no output-shape guidance. Four of five failures are silent zero-row results (sp0362 trailing space in literal + wrong column choice; sp0536 wrong degree column/value; sp0610 case-sensitive `=` on title; sp0894 friendship stored one-directionally), which an execute-and-repair loop with value probing can catch; sp0755 is an output-shape error ("which countries" → gold returns all columns). So I add: (1) control code that executes the draft and, on error/empty result, probes actual cell values for the question's literals and asks for one repair; (2) prompt rules for projection shape, trimmed/case-insensitive LIKE matching, symmetric relations, and picking the right attribute column; (3) larger token budget so reasoning plus SQL fits.

